#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# finitely_presented_group

#% text
# `finitely_presented_group([a, b, ...], [r1, ...])`: the group with these generators and relators (words as lists of letters)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Generators are symbols. A word is a list of letters `a`, `a^-1` or `a^k`; nested lists are concatenated, so `table([a, b], 5)` is the word (a b)^5. (`[a, b]^5` is the list `[a^5, b^5]`.)

#% item
# A relator is a word equal to the identity; `u -> v` states that the words u and v are equal.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
f = finitely_presented_group([a, b], [a^2, b^3, table([a, b], 5)])

#% cell
group_order(f)
#% output
#= 60

#% cell
group_order(finitely_presented_group([s, t], [table([s, t], 2) -> [s, s, s], [s, s, s] -> t^5]))
#% output
#= 120

